# [Paper published in *mSystems*]($section.id('2026-07-20'))

[Influence of heterotrophs on phage infection of marine
picocyanobacteria](https://journals.asm.org/doi/10.1128/msystems.00769-26)

Shaul's last(?) paper from his time at Penny Chisholm's lab. Allison found that
_Prochlorococcus_ only recovered from phage infection if heterotrophs were
around, but not if it grew in monoculture. 

The twist: after regrowth _Prochlorococcus_ was resistant to the phage - so far
so good - BUT! This was, to the best we could tell, not due to genetic changes.

More weirdness in the paper.

